## Business Summary- Healthcare Risk Analysis

- Problem
Healthcare models report high overall accuracy but fail to identify where predictions break down, creating hidden risk in critical decisions.

⸻

- Approach
Developed a risk-based evaluation framework to segment predictions into low, moderate, and high-risk zones based on instability and model disagreement.

⸻

- Impact
	•	Identified moderate-risk segment with highest error rate (23.9%), compared to:
	•	High-risk: 18.2%
	•	Low-risk: 5.3%
	•	Detected false negatives concentrated in moderate-risk cases (~10.9%), indicating hidden failure zones
	•	Enabled targeted human review instead of blanket automation, improving decision safety

⸻

## Key Insight
	•	Highest errors are not in obvious high-risk zones, but in moderate-risk segments
	•	Model reliability varies significantly across segments despite strong overall performance
	•	Segment-level evaluation is critical for safe deployment

⸻

## Business Relevance
	•	Supports risk-based intervention strategies in healthcare analytics
	•	Reduces likelihood of missed critical cases (false negatives)
	•	Enables responsible AI adoption with human-in-the-loop decision systems
